# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known external library leaks
#
# QtNetwork triggers libproxy proxy resolution during QNetworkAccessManager::get(),
# which allocates GLib objects that persist as cached state. These are not real
# leaks in application code — they are semi-global caches inside libproxy/glib
# that LSAN reports at process exit.
leak:libproxy
leak:libpxbackend
leak:g_list_append

# Qt's QLibrary/QLoader cache keeps plugin registration structures reachable
# from globals inside libQt6Core (an uninstrumented library), so LSAN reports
# them as indirect leaks with no application-side root. These stacks are all
# allocations made during plugin load in the two DAP-disable tests only.
leak:PluginManager::loadPluginFileAbsolute
leak:PluginHost::addDockWidget
leak:PluginHost::registerPanel
